Now render.js: els additions, render stage-6 blocks, network table rows, NX browser display override. Edits:

1. els: add dnsStats: $('dns-stats'), dnsEntries: $('dns-entries-list'), routerStats: $('router-stats'), networkRows: $('network-interfaces').
2. NX display override in activeBrowserDisplay usage.
3. renderNetworkRows + renderDnsEntries functions.
4. stage >= 6 block.

render() currently ends with:
```js
  if (snapshot.stage === 5 && snapshot.workerQueue) {...}
  renderHopHighlights(...)
```
Add after the stage-5 block:
```js
  if (snapshot.stage === 6) {
    els.dnsStats.textContent = labels.dnsStatsLabel;
    renderDnsEntries(labels.dnsEntries);
    els.routerStats.textContent = labels.routerStatsLabel;
  }
  renderNetworkRows(snapshot);
```
renderNetworkRows always (stage-dependent rows).

Browser display NX override: in render():
```js
  const display = activeBrowserDisplay(snapshot, activeAddress);
```
then used for body/badge. NX: snapshot.trace?.status === 'NX' → use pseudo-display {status:'NX', request: snapshot.trace.request, body: 'NX no record'}. Implement:

```js
  // Stage 6 NX: an unknown host never produced a wire record — the browser
  // card renders the DNS answer itself (DESIGN.md #node-dns).
  const nx = snapshot.trace?.status === 'NX' ? { status: 'NX', body: 'NX no record', request: snapshot.trace.request } : null;
  const display = nx ?? activeBrowserDisplay(snapshot, activeAddress);
```

badgeClass: 'NX' → NaN → status-err ✓. Badge text `${display.status} (${display.request})` = "NX (GET nope.example/about)" ✓.

