}
```
Careful: stage 1 interfaces: { 10.1: 'WebServer', 10.2: 'Browser (You)', Crowd }. Stage 2 adds 10.11/10.12. Stage 3 adds '10.20'. Stage 4 adds 10.30/10.31. Stage 5 adds 10.40/10.41. Stage 6 adds '10.60', 10.65, 20.1. Build incrementally to keep exact same keys/order as today (JSON key order matters? toEqual doesn't care about order; the network interfaces test checks specific keys). Existing order: 10.1, 10.11, 10.12, 10.2, then extras, Crowd last. Keep.

```js
const networkInterfaces = (snapshot) => {
  const stage = snapshot.stage ?? 1;
  const n = snapshot.users ?? 5;
  const list = {};
  if (stage === 1) {
    list[10.1] = 'WebServer';
